  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given wave equation :<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>y</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mtext>10</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>sin</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mtext>100</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext>20x</mtext><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><br />Standard equation :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>y</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a&#160;sin&#160;</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mtext>x</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Comparing the two, we obtain<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;&#160;&#160;</mo> </mrow> </math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>&nbsp;and &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>100</mtext><mtext>20</mtext></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><